      "notes": "Undergraduate race counts use the CDS B2 degree-seeking undergraduate column for 2020-2021 and 2021-2022 because Penn State did not populate the total-undergraduates column in those years. Existing 2020-2021 through 2024-2025 undergraduate residency counts were derived by applying CDS F1 undergraduate out-of-state percentages to domestic degree-seeking undergraduate enrollment and using CDS B2 nonresident counts as international because the CDS does not list explicit undergraduate in-state and out-of-state headcounts. Added 2016-2017 through 2019-2020 B2 all-undergraduate race columns are blank and are omitted; no residency counts were inferred for newly added years. Costs now use G1 undergraduate in-district tuition in every year. The 2022-2023 source prints conflicting in-district and in-state/out-of-district tuition; the explicitly reported in-district $19,286 is used, and required fees retain $549.48. G1 cost reporting periods and H2 aid reporting periods can differ from the CDS year."
